'' '-exx' CHECKS EVERY SUBSCRIPT. The call shape is fbc's, measured from its own
'' '-gen llvm -r' output on this same source:
''
''     fb_ArraySngBoundChkEx( i64 idx, i64 ubound, i32 line, ptr file, ptr name )
''
'' THE SINGLE-BOUND FORM IS FOR AN LBOUND OF 0. The runtime declares its first two
'' parameters UNSIGNED so a negative index becomes enormous and fails the one
'' 'idx > ubound' test -- one comparison instead of two, and it is why an array whose
'' lbound is not 0 takes fb_ArrayBoundChkEx and its signed triple instead.
''
'' ONE CALL PER SUBSCRIPT, so two here: the assignment reads the index once and the
'' PRINT reads it again.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -exx --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/boundchk.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: call ptr @"fb_ArraySngBoundChkEx"
'' EXPECT-OUT: declare ptr @"fb_ArraySngBoundChkEx"

'' The bound is the DECLARED one, folded in at compile time -- 9, not the element
'' count 10, and not read from a descriptor a fixed array does not have.
'' EXPECT-OUT: i64 9

'' The line the subscript sits on, so the abort can name it.
'' EXPECT-OUT: i32 3
